SLAAC

Integral component of the IPv6 protocol

Used to simplify network configuration process and make assigning IP addresses easy; Allows hosts to configure their own IP addressses autonomously and without authority

Steps:
1. Device Initiation; generates temporary link local address
2. Router Solicitation; asks for any local routers to identify themselves
3. Router Advertisement; local routers respond with information about the network and where the host fits in; THIS IS WHERE THEY PROVIDE THE PREFIX OF YOUR LOCAL NETWORK
4. Address Configuration; The device itself will combine the network prefix with its own unique identifier that derives from its hardware address to make a unique IP address
5. Final Check; performs a neighbor solicitation to make sure no one else has that IP